.TH QFW-SERVICE-PLANE 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-service-plane \- compatibility manager for a combined QFw service plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-service-plane start
.BI --run-dir " directory"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B qfw-service-plane run
.BI --run-dir " directory"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B qfw-service-plane status
.BI --run-dir " directory"
.PP
.B qfw-service-plane stop
.BI --run-dir " directory"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-service-plane
starts and manages the services used by QFw applications. A service plane may
contain a DEFw directory service, a PRTE DVM, and one QPM service.
The selected YAML files describe the requested services. The command resolves
those inputs and records the running instance under the required run directory.
.PP
New site deployments normally start the directory service independently with
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1)
and start one manager per QPM with
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1).
This allows a central directory to serve QPMs on different nodes.
.PP
The
.B start
command returns after every configured component becomes ready. The
.B run
command remains in the foreground and supervises owned components. It is the
appropriate command for systemd and other service managers.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start configured components in the background and return after readiness.
.TP
.B run
Start the service plane, remain in the foreground, and stop owned components
when SIGINT or SIGTERM is received.
.TP
.B status
Probe recorded components, update the generated state, and print it as JSON.
.TP
.B stop
Stop owned components in reverse launch order and update the generated state.
.SH START AND RUN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
Use this directory for state, readiness files, logs, and generated connection
settings. An empty value is rejected.
.TP
.BI --site-config " file"
Read site installation, directory, service-manifest, and QPM settings from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " file"
Read resolver and component-launch settings from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --profile " name"
Select an installed runtime profile when
.B --runtime-config
is omitted.
.TP
.BI --scope " application|site"
Select application-owned or site-owned service configuration. The default is
.BR site .
.TP
.BI --service-id " id"
Start the named manifest service. One service-plane instance manages exactly
one QPM, and this option may be specified only once.
.TP
.BI --service-node " node"
Start the directory service and any QPM without an explicit host on
.IR node .
The configured directory endpoint must identify the same node.
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Set the startup timeout. The default is 120 seconds.
.TP
.BI --poll-interval " seconds"
Set the component polling interval used by
.BR run .
The default is 2 seconds.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Resolve configuration and create representative state without starting
processes or reserving application-scope ports.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Component selection uses the
.B local-services
mapping in the runtime configuration. The
.BR start-prte ,
.BR start-dirsvc ,
and
.B start-qpm
keys control which components are launched.
.PP
Site scope reads its service manifest from the site configuration. Application
scope reads the manifest named by
.BR local-services.service-manifest .
If a site runtime contains no
.B local-services
mapping, the command starts a directory service and QPM without PRTE.
.PP
See
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5),
and
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5)
for the configuration formats.
.SH GENERATED FILES
.TP
.I run-dir/state/service-plane.json
Generated configuration snapshot, ownership record, process identifiers,
readiness, and lifecycle timestamps. This file is not user configuration.
.TP
.I run-dir/qfw-service-env.sh
Application-safe connection environment for clients of the service plane.
.TP
.I run-dir/services/name/pid
PID of an owned directory or QPM process.
.TP
.I run-dir/services/name/ready.json
Readiness result written after the component passes its startup probe.
.TP
.I run-dir/services/name/service-ready.json
QPM-specific readiness detail published by the service implementation.
.TP
.I run-dir/services/name/logs/
DEFw and component logs.
.TP
.I run-dir/prte_dvm/dvm-uri
PRTE rendezvous URI. This file exists only when PRTE is configured.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful startup, readiness, or shutdown. The
.B status
command returns nonzero unless the recorded service plane is ready. Startup
configuration errors, readiness timeouts, and incomplete shutdowns also return
nonzero.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a site-owned fakeIQM service plane on node c1:
.PP
.EX
qfw-service-plane start \\
  --run-dir /shared/qfw-runs/fake-iqm-site \\
  --site-config /etc/openqse/qfw/site.yaml \\
  --runtime-config /etc/openqse/qfw/runtime/fake-iqm-site.yaml \\
  --scope site \\
  --service-id fake-iqm \\
  --service-node c1
.EE
.PP
Inspect and stop the same instance:
.PP
.EX
qfw-service-plane status --run-dir /shared/qfw-runs/fake-iqm-site
qfw-service-plane stop --run-dir /shared/qfw-runs/fake-iqm-site
.EE
